      "timestamp_sec": 5095,
      "why": "A specific, checkable number underpinning the argument that code training data is exhausted."
    },
    {
      "text": "I would predict that in one year we'll let Gemini or other model generate the code and nobody will actually look at it.",
      "timestamp_sec": 5223,
      "why": "A dated, falsifiable prediction that directly contradicts the verification-first talks earlier in the day."
    },
    {
      "text": "so this led to our really big revelation what if the best way to evaluate an agent was actually with an agent",
      "timestamp_sec": 6039,
      "why": "Names the agent-as-judge position that the rest of the eval track argues over."
    },
    {
      "text": "Because benchmarks measure model capability. Production measures system behavior.",
      "timestamp_sec": 8234,
      "why": "The cleanest formulation of the offline-vs-production eval split."
    },
    {
      "text": "So more compute did not transfer the cheap structure did.",
      "timestamp_sec": 9228,
      "why": "A negative result: test-time compute scaling for retrieval did not generalize out of domain."
    },
    {
      "text": "Search is test time compute. So don't reach for bigger model. Do more search at inference instead.",
      "timestamp_sec": 9626,
      "why": "Compresses the retrieval talk's whole thesis into a prescription."
    },
    {
      "text": "Japa in just one round of reflection using just three data points is already able to get twice the performance gains that gpo got after 25,000 rollouts",
      "timestamp_sec": 20401,
      "why": "The strongest sample-efficiency claim of the day, pitting text-space optimization against RL."
    },
    {
      "text": "Token prices have continued to fall by 5 to 10x every year for each fixed level of intelligence.",
      "timestamp_sec": 29474,
      "why": "Resolves the apparent contradiction between falling prices and rising bills."
    },
    {
      "text": "The vast majority of tokens to complete longrunning agentic tasks are input tokens.",
      "timestamp_sec": 30092,
      "why": "Practical cost-modeling correction — most teams optimize output tokens instead."
    },
    {
      "text": "More AI agents running does not mean that there is more of you available. Your cognitive bandwidth does not parallelize.",
      "timestamp_sec": 28719,
      "why": "Names 'orchestration tax' as the limit on parallel-agent workflows."
    },
    {
      "text": "So here's an operational rule. Explain it or don't ship it.",
      "timestamp_sec": 28974,
      "why": "The day's most actionable governance heuristic for AI-generated code."
    }
